  "description": "JAWQAC crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H100 Cl4 Dy7 N8 O36 Zn4 1+,4(C2 H3 N1),Cl1 1-,4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.322-4.280 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.44-132.40°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Zn4Dy7(L)8(O2)2(OH)4(Cl)4(H2O)4]·Cl·4CH3CN·4H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
